A1. Better skip this—it's forbidden. ~ PROHIBITED
A10. A good place to go to sea from. ~ SHORE
A11. Titania's hubby, so Shakespeare says. ~ OBERON
A13. Rap. ~ BLAME
A14. Modern music. ~ SWING
A15. The go-between for Plaster & Paris. ~ OF
A17. One way to bring up Cain. ~ RAISE
A18. Them over here. ~ THESE
A19. A noble word. ~ SIR
A20. Every good fairy story starts thus. ~ ONCE
A21. A Big Noise in Norse deities. ~ THOR
A22. Them over there. ~ THOSE
A24. Poet's debt. ~ ODE
A25. This word is secret to us all. ~ PRIVY
A26. Aid, from a lawyer. ~ ABET
A27. You sometimes see stars after this interjection. ~ MY
A28. The only thing she missed in Wonderland was the Townsend Plan. ~ ALICE
A29. Emphasis is needed here. ~ STRESS
A31. The house that Dickens built. ~ BLEAK
A32. Something to shout about. ~ CHEER
A33. A pickup for your radio. ~ AERIAL
A35. By-products of green apples. ~ PAINS
A36. All of us. ~ WE
A38. The cross crustacean. ~ CRAB
A39. This'll probably make you mad. ~ TAUNT
A40. He just can't go straight. ~ BOA
A41. This gets in your hair. ~ TONIC
A43. Language of the Gaels, though it's nothing to blow about. ~ ERSE
A44. All sots of people hang around these. ~ BARS
A45. A queer word for anyone to use. ~ ODD
A46. Home of the high flyers. ~ AERIE
A48. This is always behindhand. ~ WRIST
A49. A business preposition. ~ RE
A50. Stony ground in South America. ~ ANDES
A51. What the dowager did to the young man with her lorgnette. ~ FROZE
A52. Powdered. ~ DUSTED
A54. Spout. ~ ORATE
A55. The music goes round and round. ~ PHONOGRAPH

D1. Pertaining to the moon. ~ PHASE
D2. Where you do as the Romans do. ~ ROME
D3. Crude metal found in Korea. ~ ORE
D4. The boy friend. ~ HE
D5. Oh, we won't go there any more! ~ BOWERY
D6. Mr. Stork's Egyptian cousin. ~ IBIS
D7. Something to hold on to. ~ TENET
D8. Amount of work done by Most W.P.A.'s. ~ ERG
D9. If you want anything repeated, put it in the middle of this. ~ DO
D10. Dangerous curve, for a golfer. ~ SLICE
D12. Rackets. ~ NOISES
D13. When the knees take a bow. ~ BANDY
D14. Lots of push here. ~ SHOVE
D16. The worries of a ukelele. ~ FRETS
D17. A place for improvement. ~ ROOM
D18. How London likes its fogs. ~ THICK
D19. There's an unreel quality about this kind of man. ~ SOBER
D21. We invite you to make this test. ~ TRIAL
D23. These forge ahead by leaps and bounds. ~ HARES
D25. A special request. ~ PLEA
D28. This is best made with cast iron. ~ ALIBI
D29. Glisten, as an unpowdered nose. ~ SHINE
D30. Just an old canvas-back. ~ TENT
D31. This makes a good impression on cattle. ~ BRAND
D32. You need this to get the effect. ~ CAUSE
D33. His daily bread consists of roles. ~ ACTOR
D34. Wore away. ~ ERODED
D35. Place to get plastered. ~ PARIS
D36. This gets badder as you go on. ~ WORSE
D37. One of the points about a compass. ~ EAST
D39. Ships get very bored by this worm. ~ TEREDO
D40. Something underhand at the billiard table. ~ BAIZE
D42. A defeeted comedian. ~ CANTO
D44. What happened when a chicken got in the soup. ~ BROTH
D47. Such a divine garden! ~ EDEN
D48. It's easy to get wrapped up in this. ~ WRAP
D50. All that was left after the big flare-up. ~ ASH
D51. The start of any frappé. ~ FRA
D53. What people try to keep with the Joneses. ~ UP
D54. This is your alternative. ~ OR


